set(v_hearing_aux,-3) if (v_b2_ch11_added_hearing == 1)
#if(v_ancient_languages == 4) {
 The flying carriages streak across the sky in a frenzy while crowds below surge along the broad avenues toward what must be the military sector. Dark blue banners hang from every facade, each emblazoned with a golden hawk clutching the sun in its talons.

A voice blares through a magical amplifier in ancient Lessathi: 'Clear the eastern district immediately. The High Council has convened in the Great Hall and will not tolerate disruption.'

Whatever is descending on this city has thrown an entire civilization into panic.

}
#if(v_ancient_languages == 0) {
 The flying carriages streak across the sky in a frenzy while crowds below surge along the broad avenues toward what must be the military sector. Dark blue banners hang from every facade, each emblazoned with a golden hawk clutching the sun in its talons.

A voice blares through a magical amplifier in a language I cannot parse.

Whatever is descending on this city has thrown an entire civilization into panic.

}
#if(v_ancient_languages == 1 || v_ancient_languages == 2 || v_ancient_languages == 3) {
 The flying carriages streak across the sky in a frenzy while crowds below surge along the broad avenues toward what must be the military sector. Dark blue banners hang from every facade, each emblazoned with a golden hawk clutching the sun in its talons.

A voice blares through a magical amplifier in ancient Lessathi, though the archaic vocabulary is too dense for my current grasp of the language.

Whatever is descending on this city has thrown an entire civilization into panic.

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_added_hearing != 0) {
 The sharpness in my ears suddenly drops. A glance at my stat booster confirms the three bonus points in Hearing granted by the override code have expired.

"I don't believe it..." Melindra murmurs, staring at the monolithic spires. "Those seredium-dusted towers match the architectural records of the ancient Lessathi empire. I've only read about them in historical archives. Even six centuries ago before the empire fell, structures of this magnitude were long gone. The relics in Ollendor are broken rubble compared to this. For towers to stand in this condition, we must be four, maybe five thousand years in the past. At the absolute height of their power. What is Selkram thinking?"

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_added_hearing == 0) {
 "I don't believe it..." Melindra murmurs, staring at the monolithic spires. "Those seredium-dusted towers match the architectural records of the ancient Lessathi empire. I've only read about them in historical archives. Even six centuries ago before the empire fell, structures of this magnitude were long gone. The relics in Ollendor are broken rubble compared to this. For towers to stand in this condition, we must be four, maybe five thousand years in the past. At the absolute height of their power. What is Selkram thinking?"

}
choice(""Never mind the history lesson. Any idea who might be attacking the city?"", B2-Ch11c-History, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-History, v_b2_ch11_towers = 0)
choice(""Should I take it that we are still in Varathia, then?"", B2-Ch11c-History, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-History, v_b2_ch11_towers = 1)
choice(""How do these towers work, exactly?"", B2-Ch11c-History, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-History, v_b2_ch11_towers = 2)


ID: B2-Ch11c-History
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch11_towers == 0) {
 "Never mind the history lesson. Any idea who might be attacking the city?"

"A rival city-state, perhaps?" Melindra says. "Lessathi history is badly fragmented, but civil wars weren't unheard of. Or perhaps an assault by primordial-era mages. We might learn more from the civic broadcasts."

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_towers == 1) {
 "Should I take it that we are still in Varathia, then?"

"It wasn't called Varathia back then, but yes—same landmass," Melindra says. "Modern cities were built over the ruins of old Lessathi hubs, and their empire existed solely on this continent."

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_towers == 2) {
 "How do these towers work, exactly?"

"From the old texts, civic mages charged the spires daily in exchange for imperial stipends," Melindra says. "That stored magical energy powered the aerial carriages, transport lifts, and technological infrastructure throughout the city."

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0 && v_ch4_spared_dave == 1) {
 "What in the hell are you two talking about?" Dave says. The updraft has dropped him to the cobblestones, and he stares up at the sky in open bewilderment. "Where are we?"

"An imperial Lessathi city, five thousand years ago," Melindra says. "Try to keep up."

"If we've been thrown into the past again, are there events we have to reenact?" Hadrik asks.

"No, this is an entirely different ritual," Arraka says from the amulet. "Look at yourselves—you were pulled through with your physical bodies, not just your minds."

"You mean we can alter the past?" Daren asks.

"No," Arraka says. "True past only changes through time reversal. This is an alternate timeline running parallel to ours where the future hasn't happened yet. Whatever we do here won't touch our reality."

"Then what is the objective of this trial?" Daren asks.

"No idea," Arraka says. "Though I know why we were sent to this exact moment."

"Explain," Illuna says.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1 || v_ch4_spared_dave == 0) {
 "If we've been thrown into the past again, are there events we have to reenact?" Hadrik asks.

"No, this is an entirely different ritual," Arraka says from the amulet. "Look at yourselves—you were pulled through with your physical bodies, not just your minds."

"You mean we can alter the past?" Daren asks.

"No," Arraka says. "True past only changes through time reversal. This is an alternate timeline running parallel to ours where the future hasn't happened yet. Whatever we do here won't touch our reality."

"Then what is the objective of this trial?" Daren asks.

"No idea," Arraka says. "Though I know why we were sent to this exact moment."

"Explain," Illuna says.

}
 "Remember how in every one of the rituals so far, Selkram has sent you to relive events from your own pasts?" Arraka says. "Well, like I said before, neither of you have lived anywhere near long enough to have experienced these current events. So by process of elimination, the past that we are now exploring is most likely... mine."

Not long after Arraka finishes speaking, the sky darkens to bruised charcoal as a suffocating, malevolent aura blankets the skyline. Metal carriages plummet from the clouds, smashing into rooftops below.

A woman descends through the gloom, clad in voluminous traditional wizard robes like the ones Azarius wears. Her eyes are pitch black, and a vicious, familiar smirk curves her lips.

"Well, well, well..." the woman says, looking toward Arraka's amulet. "Looks like Selkram sent me a gift. Travelers from the future, I take it? Let me taste my future aura... Five thousand years older, and you managed to get yourself trapped in a trinket by a circus troupe? What even is this company? A clown girl? A giant masquerading as a dwarf? A woman in sleepwear? You're competing for the most ridiculous wizarding party of the millennium."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch11c-Mountain, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-Mountain)


ID: B2-Ch11c-Mountain
TEXT:

 "I'm not dressed like a clown!" Flower shouts. "These are acrobat clothes! Acrobat clothes! How is it so hard to tell the difference?"

"Acrobat clothes!" the woman roars, her laughter splitting into the harsh harmony of three distinct voices. "This would be hilarious if it weren't so pathetic. Is this really where I end up in five millennia? Trapped in an amulet, playing lapdog to a clown? What cruel joke has fate played on me?"

"Shut your mouth, you fool!" present-Arraka roars from the amulet. "This is your one chance to fix your future! Shatter this amulet, free me, and we'll slaughter every self-proclaimed god who had a hand in banishing us! They overwhelmed us alone, but together we're unstoppable! We'll tear through the gods of this copy of a world, then break back into my reality and slaughter them all over again! Break the cage and we'll forge a force that makes even the Magium tremble!"

"The Magium?" past-Arraka sneers. "You speak of the Magium as if it were a person? What kind of senile idiot have I become over the centuries?"

"Are you freeing me or not?!"

"No," past-Arraka says, her tone hardening. "I am not freeing you. You may have gone soft with age, but I haven't lost my wits. You expect me to believe you'll play ally the moment you're out? The first thing you'll do is strike to eliminate the only entity capable of destroying you. And with five thousand years of accumulated lore, you might succeed. Why risk it? Better to leave you rotting in that box until I find a way to burn you away permanently. You have only your own incompetence to blame for getting trapped."

"Is that so?" present-Arraka snarls. "Want to know what your future holds, you arrogant wretch? You're going to spend thousands of years sealed inside a mountain! Every grand ambition of vengeance crushed! You'll be far more useless than I am right now—at least I can cast spells! You will rot in total darkness for millennia, and you deserve every second of it!"

"A mountain?" past-Arraka's grin sharpens. "How informative. So avoiding your fate is as simple as steering clear of mountains... Perhaps you have utility after all. Maybe I'll tear that chain from the girl's throat and keep you as my personal trinket, extracting every secret you've hoarded over five thousand years."

"Try it, you cheap imitation! I'll leave your carcass in ash!"

"Quiet while I butcher your companions," past-Arraka says, raising her hand. "We'll have ample time to converse once you're hanging from my neck."

choice("Attack past-Arraka with my dagger.", B2-Ch11c-Shelter, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-Shelter, v_b2_ch11_dagger = 1)
choice("Try to stall for time, in the hopes that the others can come up with a plan.", B2-Ch11c-Shelter, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-Shelter, v_b2_ch11_dagger = 0)


ID: B2-Ch11c-Shelter
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch11_madman,1) if (v_b2_ch11_dagger == 1 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch11_dagger == 0 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 0 || v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch11_dagger == 1 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 0)
achievement("Madman",v_ac_b2_ch11_madman)
#if(v_b2_ch11_dagger == 1 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1) {
 "You won't take us down that easily," I say, drawing my dagger and stepping forward.

"I'm not here for games, boy," past-Arraka says. "If I want you dead, you're dead."

She raises her hand to cast, but freezes mid-motion as the revenant locks time around everyone outside our group.

"I've frozen her..." the revenant says, pressing a hand to her temple. "The concentration won't hold long. We need shelter."

"Look for seredium-dusted buildings!" Melindra calls out. "Magical sense can't pierce seredium. We can hide there."

We sprint from the open concourse into the labyrinth of side streets, scanning the masonry for black dust.

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_dagger == 0 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1) {
 "Are you sure you want to kill us?" I say. "Present-Arraka won't tell you anything, but the rest of us have traveled with her for months. We know her secrets. We can trade that knowledge for our freedom."

"Nerves of steel, boy," past-Arraka says, her malicious grin returning. "But what could you possibly offer that--"

She freezes mid-sentence as the revenant locks time around everyone outside our group.

"I've frozen her..." the revenant says, pressing a hand to her temple. "The concentration won't hold long. We need shelter."

"Look for seredium-dusted buildings!" Melindra calls out. "Magical sense can't pierce seredium. We can hide there."

We sprint from the open concourse into the labyrinth of side streets, scanning the masonry for black dust.

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_dagger == 0 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 0) {
 "Are you sure you want to kill us?" I say. "Present-Arraka won't tell you anything, but the rest of us have traveled with her for months. We know her secrets. We can trade that knowledge for our freedom."

"Nerves of steel, boy," past-Arraka says, her malicious grin returning. "But what could you possibly offer that I couldn't pry from your corpse?"

"Events from your future that went disastrously wrong," I say. "Wouldn't you prefer the advantage of foreknowledge? It costs us nothing—this timeline isn't ours."

"A tempting pitch, if your stalling weren't so transparent, boy," past-Arraka sneers. "You're waiting for your time weaver to freeze the field. It won't work. The moment I arrived, I cast an aura-disruption ward across the district specifically targeting temporal manipulation. Your weaver has been fighting a crippling migraine for the past minute. Your delay tactics are completely useless--"

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_dagger == 1 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 0) {
 "You won't take us down that easily," I say, drawing my dagger and stepping forward.

"I'm not here for games, boy," past-Arraka says. "If I want you dead, you're dead."

She flicks her wrist. Desiccation magic tears through my body, drying flesh to ash as my vision grays out.

"And don't bother attempting a rewind, weaver," Arraka's voice fades into the dark. "I blanketed the area in anti-temporal wards. Your friend is dust, and you will follow him."

I collapse into dust as consciousness blacks out completely.

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1 && v_ch4_spared_dave == 1) {
 "I am going to tear that imposter apart!" present-Arraka shrieks from the amulet as we sprint through the alleys. "If I had a body, I'd rip her in two and feed her to dogs!"

"Arraka, scan for walls opaque to your magical sense!" Illuna shouts.

"Right—let me look," Arraka says. "Yes, there's one ahead. Take a left at the next crossroads and sprint straight. I'll call the turn."

"Can't Melindra fly us?" I ask between strides.

"We run faster than her carry speed," Kate says.

"The road is clear, just keep moving," Arraka says.

"Where did the cutthroat run off to?" Daren asks.

"Bolted the opposite direction the second time froze," Arraka says. "Smart move—my past self is hunting us, not him."

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1 && v_ch4_spared_dave == 0) {
 "I am going to tear that imposter apart!" present-Arraka shrieks from the amulet as we sprint through the alleys. "If I had a body, I'd rip her in two and feed her to dogs!"

"Arraka, scan for walls opaque to your magical sense!" Illuna shouts.

"Right—let me look," Arraka says. "Yes, there's one ahead. Take a left at the next crossroads and sprint straight. I'll call the turn."

"Can't Melindra fly us?" I ask between strides.

"We run faster than her carry speed," Kate says.

"The road is clear, just keep moving," Arraka says.

}
#if(v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1) {
 Mid-sprint, the revenant stumbles, clutching her head as the stasis breaks. Once time snaps forward, it takes past-Arraka less than three seconds to teleport directly into our path, cutting off the alley.

"Such a pity," past-Arraka purrs. "You were nearly to cover. Surprising that your weaver held the freeze as long as she did under my anti-temporal ward. Dizziness protection, I presume? No matter. She is drained, and your run is over--"

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch11c-Avalanche, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11c-Avalanche) if (v_b2_ch11_dagger == 0 || v_b2_ch11_echoes == 1)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b2_ch11_dagger == 1 && v_b2_ch11_echoes == 0)
